// HumanityOS OPENING STYLES -- door/window animation styles the construction editor offers.
// The opening stores the chosen id; crates/humanity-systems/src/door_anim.rs animates from it. Add a
// style by adding a row here (infinite-of-x): the editor lists every entry, and an AI can enumerate
// them, so this file IS the source of truth for "what opening styles exist". Compile-time embedded
// (door_anim::opening_styles); a change here needs a rebuild.
//
// anchors (character animation rung 2b, 2026-11-10): the interaction anchors a door of this style
// offers, ids of data/characters/interactions.ron. A swing door's handle: a person going through
// closes a hand round it while the door swings open.
//
// hand (the operator, 2026-11-10: "Sure."): a HAND opens a door of this style instead of it opening
// by itself at its open_dist (door_anim::HandOpen). It starts to swing when a walking person's feet
// come within reach_m of its handle (their hand on it: 0.40 m is where the shortest body's arm reaches
// a handle at 0.95 m from its feet on the handle's side; the operator was asked about "about 0.9 m",
// the distance the hand starts reaching from) or within touch_m of its face anywhere across
// its width (just short of the body touching it, so nobody stands stuck at a shut door), swings away
// from them (they stand inside the arc a panel coming toward them would sweep) at the push's pace
// (swing_rate per second, against 9 for a door that opens itself: about a walking pace at the
// handle, so the hand stays on it) and stops blocking the walk once it moves. A sprint (faster than
// sprint_mps across the floor) and an animal still open it at its open_dist, so nobody runs into it
// shut.
[
    (id: "swing", anchors: ["door_swing_handle"], hand: Some((reach_m: 0.40, touch_m: 0.42, swing_rate: 1.0, sprint_mps: 5.5))),
    (id: "slide"),
    (id: "iris"),
    (id: "rotate"),
    (id: "fold"),
    (id: "energy"),
    (id: "nanowall"),
    (id: "fixed"),
]
